  "tiledMaterials": {
    "why": "G641: the materials a tiled plot (an idea row with a layout, generators/tiledPlot.mjs) adds to the look: the kit's lit vertex colours, its lanterns and windows, and the landmark's own texture. The landmark draws its own texture alone: its vertex colours carry that texture's colours for the views that sample no texture (the near view, the map). NM7: pool is the warm light under every lantern and round the gate, added over the paving (its colour falls to black at the rim); glow runs brighter so lanterns, string lights and awnings read as lit. NM8: water is its own glossy surface (low roughness, a strong environment) so the sky and the lights' glow sit in the canals.",
